        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add bounded PR detail fill command",
        "body": "Closes #83.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAdds a bounded `fill-pr-details` workflow for hydrating missing pull-request detail rows without allowing one started batch to consume through an operator's configured GitHub rate-limit reserve.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe command selects missing rows in ordered batches, bootstraps the relevant core and GraphQL quotas, and reserves quota before each request dispatched by that fill invocation. Reserve-enabled runs fail closed on redirects and stop cleanly at the threshold; ordinary sync behavior is unchanged.\n\nThe guarantee covers requests issued by this command invocation. Other tools or invocations sharing the same token remain outside its accounting.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can backfill missing PR details with bounded selection, progress output, and a strict per-invocation quota reserve. If a batch reaches the reserve, the command stops before the next request and does not persist partial PR-detail state.\n\n## Evidence\n\nA reserve-crossing regression starts at `reserve + 1`, permits one repository request, blocks the next request at the configured reserve, reports `rate-limit-reserve`, and confirms no PR-detail row was partially persisted.",
